    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d320">

                <pb facs="0500" n="424" xml:id="pg424"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">548.D1/251</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 979</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-10-03">October 3, 1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received the Embassy’s
                    despatch No. 1616 of August 6, 1935,<anchor n="78" xml:id="d320-f1"/> with its
                    enclosure, a communication dated August 3, 1935,<anchor n="78" xml:id="d320-f2"
                    /> addressed to the Secretary of State by the Secretary General of the High
                    Commission for Refugees (Jewish and Other) coming from Germany, in which
                    information was requested concerning the documentation of refugees, their
                    permits to work in the countries to which they proceed, and other related
                    questions.</p>
                <p>You are requested to transmit to the Secretary General the attached memorandum,
                    which has been prepared by the Visa Division of the Department.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William
                            Phillips</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d320-a1.xml" xpointer="d320-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
